    nb.metadata={'kernelspec':{'display_name':'Python 3','language':'python','name':'python3'},'language_info':{'name':'python','version':'3.12'}};path=OUT/'Dance_Research_Notebook.ipynb';nbf.write(nb,path);NotebookClient(nb,timeout=120,kernel_name='python3',resources={'metadata':{'path':str(OUT)}}).execute();nbf.write(nb,path)
    page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Dance mapping · overnight results</title><style>body{{margin:0;background:#f4f3ee;color:#213c34;font:17px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif}}main{{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:40px 28px 80px}}h1{{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,62px);line-height:1.05;max-width:960px;margin:18px 0 24px}}h2{{font-size:28px;margin-top:44px}}p{{max-width:920px}}a{{color:#16745e}}video,img{{width:100%;border-radius:14px;background:#101719}}.tag{{text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.14em;font-size:12px;color:#55776a}}.lead{{font-size:21px}}.card{{background:white;padding:23px 28px;border-radius:14px;margin:20px 0}}.warn{{border-left:4px solid #b28a43}}.links{{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px}}.links a{{background:#1d6655;color:white;padding:10px 16px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:15px}}td,th{{padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #dce4df;text-align:left}}.scroll{{overflow-x:auto}}small,.muted{{color:#64776d}}summary{{cursor:pointer;font-weight:650}}li{{margin:7px 0}}</style><main><div class="tag">Overnight experiment · 10 November 2026</div><h1>Better floor points.<br>Smoother stage trajectories.</h1><p class="lead">The learned support point improves the map. Long overlaps and seated groups still break detection and identity tracking.</p><div class="links"><a href="Dance_Research_Notebook.ipynb">Research notebook</a><a href="CVAT_Review/GUIDE.html">Teammate labeling guide</a><a href="REPRODUCE.txt">Reproduce the experiment</a></div><h2>Watch the final reserved comparison</h2><p>Same person boxes, IDs, visibility decisions, and trajectory filter. Only the point changes: box bottom on the left, learned floor support on the right. Settings were frozen before this section was labeled.</p><video controls preload="metadata" poster="videos/final_reserved_070.jpg" src="videos/final_reserved.mp4"></video><div class="card scroll">{final_table}<small>Percentages are distance tolerances relative to mat width. Missing positions remain in the denominator. Seven correlated frames from one short crowd section; assistant reference labels require human review.</small></div><h2>What changed overnight</h2><div class="card"><ol><li>Expanded support training to56 varied frames and913 usable dancer crops.</li><li>Compared23 support training runs, two detector fine-tunes, identity association and multiple filters.</li><li>Kept YOLO for boxes; trained a separate support-point and visibility model.</li><li>Replaced the changing local-window smoother with a robust whole-trajectory fit.</li><li>Preserved each frozen test and added a longer stress test.</li></ol></div><h2>First reserved test</h2><div class="card scroll">{first_table}<small>Complete pipeline comparison: detector, tracking, support estimator and filter changed. A separate same-pipeline ablation scored80/135 with box bottoms and110/135 with learned support.</small></div><p>The moving/crowded phase improved from20 to40 correct positions out of55. Four of24 hidden references were incorrectly reported as measured, versus two before. The causal option had worse large-error cases; the recommended prototype processes recorded video offline.</p><details><summary>Watch the first frozen result and smoother diagnostic replay</summary><p>The second video reuses an inspected section, so it is a diagnostic rather than another heldout test.</p><video controls preload="none" src="videos/reserved_offline.mp4"></video><video controls preload="none" src="videos/round2_diagnostic.mp4"></video></details><h2>The full97-second stress test</h2><p>One reviewed initialization at176.8s, tracking in both time directions. This replay includes training frames. The left side uses the same new detector with the earlier box-map logic; it is not the old-detector baseline above.</p><video controls preload="metadata" poster="videos/full_section_1212.jpg" src="videos/full_section.mp4"></video><div class="card warn"><strong>This does not yet give twenty reliable positions throughout.</strong><p>When dancers overlap or sit together, some bodies disappear from detection and some IDs stop matching. A smooth estimate is still an estimate. Solid dots are model outputs; hollow dots are estimates; unknown positions are omitted. The mat dimensions are relative, not surveyed meters.</p></div><h2>What teammates should label</h2><p>Review the prepared person boxes, visible support points and visible/hidden/airborne/uncertain statuses. Split56 training frames as19/19/18. Keep the nine development frames separate. Do not start labeling all2,424 extracted frames.</p><img src="figures/label_examples.jpg" alt="Eight examples of floor-contact labels"><p>Segmentation alone cannot identify the supporting limb. For this experiment, boxes plus a support point and visibility status are the useful labels. Before detector retraining, also check that every distinguishable dancer has a box. Image-local IDs train support estimation; consistent short tracks are needed for identity training.</p><h2>Read the evidence</h2><div class="links"><a href="reserved_evaluation/results.json">First frozen scores</a><a href="backup_evaluation/results.json">Final reserved scores</a><a href="diagnostics/reserved_ablations.json">Point ablation</a><a href="round2/trajectory_search.json">Trajectory search</a></div><p class="muted">The notebook contains the data split, training curves, evaluation definitions, runtime scope, limitations and source links. The CVAT pack is prepared locally and has not been uploaded to your account during this overnight run.</p></main></html>'''
    for a,b in [('to56','to 56'),('and913','and 913'),('Compared23','Compared 23'),('from20','from 20'),('to40','to 40'),('of55','of 55'),('of24','of 24'),('full97','full 97'),('at176','at 176'),('Split56','Split 56'),('as19','as 19'),('all2,424','all 2,424'),('scored80','scored 80'),('and110','and 110')]:page=page.replace(a,b)
    page=page.replace('<h2>What changed overnight</h2>',f'<p>The stricter 1% score improves from {box["correct_by_tolerance_pct_width"]["1"]} to {second["correct_by_tolerance_pct_width"]["1"]} correct positions out of 77. At 3%, the gain is small ({box["correct_by_tolerance_pct_width"]["3"]} to {second["correct_by_tolerance_pct_width"]["3"]}), and the large-error tail is worse. This is progress, not a solved twenty-dancer tracker.</p><h2>What changed overnight</h2>')
    page=page.replace('Watch the final reserved comparison','Watch the second reserved comparison').replace('Final reserved scores','Second reserved scores').replace('<h2>What teammates should label</h2>',late_html+'<h2>What teammates should label</h2>')
    page=page.replace('Split 56 training frames as 19/19/18. Keep the nine development frames separate.','Split 60 training frames as 20/20/20. Keep the eleven development frames separate.')
    page=page.replace('Split 60 training frames as 20/20/20. Keep the eleven development frames separate.','Use three separate CVAT packs: 20 training images each, plus 4 / 4 / 3 validation images. Preserve the split tags and keep validation out of training.')
    latest=OUT/'final_confirmation/results.json'
    if latest.exists():
        r=read(latest);a=r['candidates']['Expanded support']['all'];b=r['candidates']['Selected pipeline / box bottom']['all'];old=r['candidates']['Incumbent support']['all'];n=a['visible_references']
        hero=f'<h2>Start with the newest point comparison</h2><p>On a newly labeled floor-work block, the expanded pipeline placed <strong>{a["correct_by_tolerance_pct_width"]["3"]}/{n}</strong> visible contacts within 3% of mat width. Box bottoms in the same pipeline placed {b["correct_by_tolerance_pct_width"]["3"]}/{n}; the established pipeline placed {old["correct_by_tolerance_pct_width"]["3"]}/{n}. Missing positions count as misses. Settings were frozen before these seven images were labeled.</p><video controls preload="metadata" poster="videos/final_confirmation_point_ablation_065.jpg" src="videos/final_confirmation_point_ablation.mp4"></video><p>These are approximate assistant reference labels. The improvement is useful, but the system still misses contacts and does not maintain twenty trustworthy positions through every overlap.</p><details><summary>Compare the established and expanded pipelines</summary><video controls preload="none" src="videos/final_confirmation.mp4"></video></details>'
        page=page.replace('<h2>Watch the second reserved comparison</h2>',hero+'<h2>Earlier frozen comparison</h2>')
        page=page.replace('The left side uses the same new detector with the earlier box-map logic; it is not the old-detector baseline above.','The left side is the established support pipeline; the right adds the development-selected detector and expanded support model.')
